[2026-09-26T19:05:16.461+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "specification": "MATERIALIZED SKELETON (router file). Contract: request body { username, email, password, confirmPassword, agreeToTerms }; success 201 { user: { id, username, email, emailVerified: true } } plus a session cookie so the account is immediately sign-in capable; failure 400 (missing/format/terms/password/confirmation) or 409 (username or email conflict) with body { message: string, fieldErrors: Partial<Record<'username'|'email'|'password'|'confirmPassword'|'agreeToTerms', string>> }. All contributing fields must be present in one response (no first-error-only). Exact visible strings: 'Username already exists', 'Username format is invalid', 'Email format is invalid', 'Password requirements are not satisfied', 'Agree to terms is required'. Passwords must never be echoed in the response. The route only mediates HTTP; validation and persistence live in FUNC/DB interfaces.",
