[2026-09-26T19:21:00.670+08:00] [TestDrivenDeveloper][REQ-1-1-1] 
[2026-09-26T19:21:00.670+08:00] [TestDrivenDeveloper][REQ-1-1-1] 1. `frontend/src/api/index.ts` uses `baseURL: '/api'` while `authApi` calls absolute `'/api/...'` paths → real runtime would hit `/api/api/...` (breaks E2E; tests mock the client so they miss it).
[2026-09-26T19:21:00.670+08:00] [TestDrivenDeveloper][REQ-1-1-1] 2. `authApi` only maps *thrown* errors, so a resolved non-2xx response is treated as success (the register page's duplicate-username path).
[2026-09-26T19:21:00.670+08:00] [TestDrivenDeveloper][REQ-1-1-1] 3. Registering while an authenticated session exists must not hijack that durable session (E2E scenario: rejected registration "leaves the original state unchanged").
[2026-09-26T19:21:00.670+08:00] [TestDrivenDeveloper][REQ-1-1-1] 4. E2E field helper uses a non-exact label match, so `getByLabel('Password')` also matches the "Confirm password" wrapper.
